00:04:50.641 --> 00:04:51.982
- My name's Darby Aldaco.

00:04:51.982 --> 00:04:54.277
I am the pastry chef here at Proof Bakery,

00:04:54.277 --> 00:04:57.027
and today we're gonna serve
you an espresso chocolate cake.

00:04:57.027 --> 00:04:59.527
- So walk us through that
process, building that cake.

00:04:59.527 --> 00:05:01.458
- First off, we make
the devil's food cake.

00:05:01.458 --> 00:05:04.101
They're trimmed, broken
down into three layers.

00:05:04.101 --> 00:05:05.184
First layer, soak.

00:05:05.184 --> 00:05:08.029
It's basically a little
espresso sugar water.

00:05:08.029 --> 00:05:10.487
Cremeux, which is a creamy pudding.

00:05:10.487 --> 00:05:12.325
We cook ours a little
bit further than normal.

00:05:12.325 --> 00:05:13.728
We take it almost to the breaking point,

00:05:13.728 --> 00:05:16.166
so it's really thick
because we actually use it

00:05:16.166 --> 00:05:18.603
as an icing as well, so
it's gotta be really thick.

00:05:18.603 --> 00:05:20.415
Next is the espresso buttercream.

00:05:20.415 --> 00:05:22.440
And then just build again,
repeat the whole process.

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:24.326
And then we crumb coat it,

00:05:24.326 --> 00:05:26.287
which basically protects the whole cake,

00:05:26.287 --> 00:05:29.069
so when you ice it, none
of the crumbs fall out.

00:05:29.069 --> 00:05:32.099
And then glaze them right before
they go out into the store.

00:05:32.099 --> 00:05:34.746
We save all the scraps that we
cut off the cakes, actually.

00:05:34.746 --> 00:05:37.208
Those get baked, dried
out, and we grind those

00:05:37.208 --> 00:05:38.990
for the crumbs that go
on the side of the cake.

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:41.538
Pretty much our biggest seller
here, besides our croissants.

00:05:41.538 --> 00:05:43.988
Its not overly sweet,
it's not overly powerful.

00:05:43.988 --> 00:05:45.287
The espresso, it's just balance.

00:05:45.287 --> 00:05:46.319
And we serve it at room temp.

00:05:46.319 --> 00:05:48.126
Otherwise, the flavors
get muddled in the cold.

00:05:48.126 --> 00:05:49.801
I think you need to have all the flavors

00:05:49.801 --> 00:05:51.834
