00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:55.943
- A day, yes.

00:08:55.943 --> 00:08:59.850
Macarons are probably our
most popular sweet item here.

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:00.683
(chuckles)

00:09:00.683 --> 00:09:01.705
- We're getting those.

00:09:01.705 --> 00:09:03.446
And so, we're gonna be eating the cake.

00:09:03.446 --> 00:09:04.419
Tell us a little bit about your process.

00:09:04.419 --> 00:09:06.211
- So if you want a cake
from Bottega Louie,

00:09:06.211 --> 00:09:09.310
we will sit down, eat
cake, discuss details,

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:11.521
have some coffee, maybe some champagne.

00:09:11.521 --> 00:09:13.623
And during the consultation,

00:09:13.623 --> 00:09:16.779
you get to taste 10 varieties of fillings,

00:09:16.779 --> 00:09:19.112
along with our chocolate
and vanilla cakes.

00:09:19.112 --> 00:09:20.651
- So Steven's already done all this.

00:09:20.651 --> 00:09:21.484
- Yes.

00:09:21.484 --> 00:09:22.317
- This already happened.

00:09:22.317 --> 00:09:23.150
- Yes.

00:09:23.150 --> 00:09:24.127
- You guys are already best friends.

00:09:24.127 --> 00:09:24.960
- Yes, we are.

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:25.919
- I'm the one out of the loop.

00:09:25.919 --> 00:09:27.688
- So then we'll go into baking the cake

00:09:27.688 --> 00:09:30.056
once the sketch has been
approved by the client.

00:09:30.056 --> 00:09:31.936
So we bake cakes, allow them to cool.

00:09:31.936 --> 00:09:34.028
During that process, we'll
be making all the decor,

00:09:34.028 --> 00:09:37.773
whether it's sugar flowers,
ribbons, bows, lace.

00:09:37.773 --> 00:09:40.214
Everything is done out
of an edible medium.

00:09:40.214 --> 00:09:43.353
Once all of the decorative
aspects are completed,

00:09:43.353 --> 00:09:46.133
the cake is filled and iced and stacked.

00:09:46.133 --> 00:09:49.039
Then at that point, we
just put it all together.

00:09:49.039 --> 00:09:50.648
Your cake, I firmly believe,

00:09:50.648 --> 00:09:52.506
has to taste as good as it looked.

00:09:52.506 --> 00:09:55.020
So our cakes start at $9 per person,

00:09:55.020 --> 00:09:57.668
and they can go up depending on

00:09:57.668 --> 00:09:59.987
how intricate and detailed the design is.

00:09:59.987 --> 00:10:04.757
So the final price tag for your
cake turns out to be $1,120.

00:10:04.757 --> 00:10:05.856
- [Steven] That is the most expensive food

00:10:05.856 --> 00:10:06.944
we've eaten on this show.

00:10:06.944 --> 00:10:07.777
- [James] To date.

00:10:07.777 --> 00:10:09.539
- [Steven] And what does
cake symbolize for you?

00:10:09.539 --> 00:10:12.166
- [James] Cake just
symbolizes life, celebration.

00:10:12.166 --> 00:10:14.999
For me, when I think about cake,
it puts a smile on my face,

00:10:14.999 --> 00:10:17.100
and I think that's how it
should be for everyone else.

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:20.085
- This is a, I've never
seen a cake like this.

00:10:20.085 --> 00:10:22.912
It is very satisfying to look at.

00:10:22.912 --> 00:10:25.138
- In case you were
wondering where the cake is,

00:10:25.138 --> 00:10:26.854
the box is the cake.

00:10:26.854 --> 00:10:27.687
- [James] The box is the cake.

00:10:27.687 --> 00:10:28.578
(chuckles)

00:10:28.578 --> 00:10:29.866
- Yeah, I guessed that.

00:10:29.866 --> 00:10:32.846
Let's see what's inside,
what mysteries it holds.

00:10:32.846 --> 00:10:35.130
- [James] This is the
best part right here.

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:37.964
- [Andrew] I love how
perfectly square everything is.

00:10:37.964 --> 00:10:39.131
- To Worth It.

00:10:40.421 --> 00:10:42.964
- So what kind of cake
did you select for us?

00:10:42.964 --> 00:10:44.608
This is partially your

00:10:44.608 --> 00:10:45.441
- Yes.

00:10:45.441 --> 00:10:46.274
- Your ideas.

00:10:46.274 --> 00:10:48.183
- What I told him was
make it fun, exciting.

00:10:48.183 --> 00:10:51.810
I told him that you are very
hard to please, which is

00:10:51.810 --> 00:10:54.379
- Relative to you, you
are very easy to please.

00:10:54.379 --> 00:10:56.804
- I'm a happy person. Is that okay?

00:10:56.804 --> 00:10:58.107
- It's fine.

00:10:58.107 --> 00:10:59.158
Let's get to the cake.

00:10:59.158 --> 00:11:00.460
- [Steven] The gift box cake.

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:02.514
It's a funfetti, strawberry buttercream

00:11:02.514 --> 00:11:03.982
and white chocolate buttercream,

00:11:03.982 --> 00:11:05.926
with a flavor explosion in the end.

00:11:05.926 --> 00:11:08.876
- I can't wait to eat
everything on this box.

00:11:08.876 --> 00:11:13.274
We've got 80 people worth of
cake and we're sharing a slice.

00:11:13.274 --> 00:11:15.722
I love that it's not just
an object sitting there.

00:11:15.722 --> 00:11:18.687
It's like a still life from a scene.

00:11:18.687 --> 00:11:19.520
- Boop.

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:23.270
(classical orchestral music)

00:11:27.118 --> 00:11:28.759
- [Steven] Strawberry galore.

00:11:28.759 --> 00:11:29.624
- It is like a delicious

00:11:29.624 --> 00:11:31.722
strawberry shortcake with sprinkles.

00:11:31.722 --> 00:11:32.968
- Take me back to my childhood.

00:11:32.968 --> 00:11:35.981
10-year-old Steven would've
went ham on this cake.

00:11:35.981 --> 00:11:37.564
Can you imagine 10-year-old Steven though?

00:11:37.564 --> 00:11:39.715
- I'm just imagining a
smaller version of you.

00:11:39.715 --> 00:11:42.463
- Mm, I'm getting that
sugar rush right now.

00:11:42.463 --> 00:11:44.753
- Yeah, I'm getting that
sugar rush right now too.

00:11:44.753 --> 00:11:48.308
- The strawberry's a very
fresh strawberry flavor.

00:11:48.308 --> 00:11:50.055
It's like I'm sucking them
right out of the field.

00:11:50.055 --> 00:11:51.958
- Let's eat some of the candies.

00:11:51.958 --> 00:11:52.791
- Sure.

00:11:54.152 --> 00:11:55.967
- No, my candy.

00:11:55.967 --> 00:11:57.944
- Yummy, it's like a
little chocolate whopper.

00:11:57.944 --> 00:11:59.867
I want you to break it
off like a wishbone.

00:11:59.867 --> 00:12:01.980
- Oh cool. You gonna wish?

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:02.835
- Sure.

00:12:02.835 --> 00:12:05.108
- Alright. What was your wish?

00:12:05.108 --> 00:12:06.691
- Didn't come true.

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:09.050
- [Steven] Tastes like decoration.

00:12:09.050 --> 00:12:11.112
- It's fun to eat something
that's shaped like this.

00:12:11.112 --> 00:12:14.434
It's like a dried pasta
noodle that's sweet.

00:12:14.434 --> 00:12:15.767
- [Steven] Whoa.

00:12:17.144 --> 00:12:18.585
I'm eating

00:12:18.585 --> 00:12:19.665
- [Andrew] It tastes like paper.

00:12:19.665 --> 00:12:20.748
- I call the party hat.

00:12:20.748 --> 00:12:22.665
- Do you wanna wear it?

00:12:24.581 --> 00:12:25.665
Party time.

00:12:25.665 --> 00:12:29.875
(classical orchestral music)

00:12:29.875 --> 00:12:31.008
- This is the most fun.

00:12:31.008 --> 00:12:32.773
Just eating whatever I want to eat,

00:12:32.773 --> 00:12:34.320
and having no consequences,

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:36.357
except for the massive
sugar rush I'm having.

00:12:36.357 --> 00:12:38.846
- Disclaimer: There
are not no consequences

00:12:38.846 --> 00:12:40.333
to eating a lot of cake.

00:12:40.333 --> 00:12:41.166
This cake is delicious,

00:12:41.166 --> 00:12:44.249
but it is very clearly
a cake inspired by you.

00:12:44.249 --> 00:12:45.368
- Tell me more.

00:12:45.368 --> 00:12:47.736
- Two kinds of cream, eight layers,

00:12:47.736 --> 00:12:49.986
sprinkles in there as well,

00:12:50.839 --> 00:12:53.514
other kind of sugar bobbles everywhere.

00:12:53.514 --> 00:12:56.106
It's like the lucid dream Steven cakes.

00:12:56.106 --> 00:13:00.258
(classical orchestral music)

00:13:00.258 --> 00:13:01.591
You like that?

00:13:01.591 --> 00:13:02.964
It's good cake, eh?

00:13:02.964 --> 00:13:04.117
What am I, Canadian?

00:13:04.117 --> 00:13:06.787
- The final question: Does
it taste as good as it look?

00:13:06.787 --> 00:13:08.342
I would say better.

00:13:08.342 --> 00:13:12.312
I would say, I think I'm
in-cake-able of eating any more.

00:13:12.312 --> 00:13:14.812
Alright, let's get outta here.

00:13:16.862 --> 00:13:18.172
Pshew.

00:13:18.172 --> 00:13:19.306
- Ooh.

00:13:19.306 --> 00:13:20.650
My heart is ready.

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:21.483
Cheers.

00:13:25.108 --> 00:13:27.346
Which one was the most
worth it at its price?

00:13:27.346 --> 00:13:28.437
- Let me break it down.

00:13:28.437 --> 00:13:30.007
Bottega Louie, amazing.

00:13:30.007 --> 00:13:32.160
I've never seen a cake
like that in my life.

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:34.323
Overall though, Proof was
the most worth it for me.

00:13:34.323 --> 00:13:36.816
It was a perfect cake in the way that

00:13:36.816 --> 00:13:38.977
you've actually had cake
when you were a little kid.

00:13:38.977 --> 00:13:42.297
- We spent over a thousand
dollars on a cake at Bottega.

00:13:42.297 --> 00:13:45.386
I truly loved Bottega:
the experience, James.

00:13:45.386 --> 00:13:47.799
All that being said,
this is the hardest one.

00:13:47.799 --> 00:13:50.643
My Worth It winner goes to Porto's.

00:13:50.643 --> 00:13:53.002
They bust out thousands of those cakes

00:13:53.002 --> 00:13:56.206
and each one is the same amazing quality.

00:13:56.206 --> 00:13:57.115
We have one more task,

00:13:57.115 --> 00:13:59.455
and now we must deliver this
to the Tasty headquarters.

00:13:59.455 --> 00:14:01.209
So are you guys ready?

00:14:01.209 --> 00:14:04.876
(cheerful orchestral music)

00:14:20.486 --> 00:14:21.736
- [Man] Oh yes.

00:14:23.956 --> 00:14:26.789
(slow rock music)

